# FAILURE MODE 5 — 401 on everything.
#
# Symptom: the stack comes up healthy (the healthcheck hits /health, which is
# exempt), the home page renders, and then EVERY call fails. Until Session 15
# this surfaced in the business backend as a raw Rails 500 page, because
# EstimatorAi::Unauthorized escaped the guard_* wrappers — fixed in the live
# session, and the reason the flash now names the variable to check.
#
# Cause: the two services hold DIFFERENT values for the shared secret. The AI
# service compares with secrets.compare_digest and rejects.
#
# The confusing variant: leaving AI_SERVICE_TOKEN EMPTY on the AI service
# disables the middleware entirely, so everything works and the guard is simply
# not there. Silence is not proof that the door is locked.
#
# Fix: one value, one place. Both services read the same root .env.
#   openssl rand -hex 32

# What the AI service validates
AI_SERVICE_TOKEN=b7e3f1a9c2d84e6f0a1b3c5d7e9f0a1b

# BROKEN: what the business backend sends (note the last characters)
BUSINESS_BACKEND_AI_SERVICE_TOKEN=b7e3f1a9c2d84e6f0a1b3c5d7e9f0a99
